Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 18:23:20 2026 +1100

    Import migrations only when syncing on startup
    
    placement.deploy imports the migration module, and so alembic, at module
    level, but update_database() only needs it when
    [placement_database]/sync_on_startup is set, which is off by default.
    Import it there, and test that importing deploy does not load alembic.
    
    Importing placement.wsgi, placement.deploy and placement.handler now
    uses 73MB of anonymous memory, not 82MB.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for import-memory fixes that can be landed one at a
    time and measured in devstack CI; placement loads alembic in every API
    process although it migrates only when asked to.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (medium effort)
    
    Depends-On: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/devstack/+/1011992
    Change-Id: I0cb82d1c407fb35059b6d1a4386006fd02cfdc45
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

